#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110494 :question/id #uuid "7c937587-dc81-5ee9-aa66-a509a87433e2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4067" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $2^{x+1}=3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_2$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x+1} & =3 \\\\ {log}_{2}⁡({2}^{x+1}) & ={log}_{2}⁡(3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b \\left( b^c \\right) = c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\nx+1 = \\log_2 \\left( 3 \\right).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1 & ={log}_{2}⁡(3) \\\\ x & ={log}_{2}⁡(3)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x= \\log_2 \\left( 3 \\right) - 1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110495 :question/id #uuid "45d74b50-fd9d-5d18-835d-a7e140278a34" :question/math-academy-id "e-4069" :question/problem "Given that $3^{2x+3}=5,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_3$ of both sides of the equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n   \t3^{2x+3} \t\t\t\t&= 5 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\\log_3 \\left(3^{2x+3}\\right)\t&= \\log_3 (5) \\\\[3pt]\n\t2x+3 \t\t\t\t\t&= \\log_3 (5) . \\\\[3pt]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+3 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}-3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx \\approx -0.768\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n**Note:** We used the change of base formula to rewrite the right-hand side, as many calculators can only compute base $10$ logarithms."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110496 :question/id #uuid "5d31a3e8-aae6-50b5-9ce1-65cef1d8395e" :question/math-academy-id "e-4071" :question/problem "Given that $3\\cdot 6^{x} = 9,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the exponential on the left-hand side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot {6}^{x} & =9 \\\\ {6}^{x} & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n   \t6^x \t\t\t\t\t&= 3 \\\\[3pt]\n\t\\log_6 \\left(6^x\\right)\t&= \\log_6 (3) \\\\[3pt]\n\tx \t\t\t\t\t&= \\log_6 (3)\\\\[3pt]\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{\\log(3)}{\\log(6)}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx \\approx 0.613\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "884debd0-06dc-5b2d-97b8-71be0323d8d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.792" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107244} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e7fe1d-4f6d-5f8d-bc9f-d91c1dd243c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.584" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107245} {:answer/id #uuid "daa2c193-3a81-549e-8222-77ce50475286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.832" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107246} {:answer/id #uuid "4477bab9-054f-5075-ba77-ef76c798f9fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.896" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107247} {:answer/id #uuid "4eed4251-80d5-59da-a48b-07a51f690d02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.916" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107248}] :answer-field/id #uuid "ba575665-f5d4-5ee1-af7f-f80bb683bdca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107243}] :question/id #uuid "438d7361-30a7-5f46-bb6b-2f800b96cdf9" :question/m