:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y={log}_{4}⁡(11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544593} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a67648-6807-50b6-a6d7-45ce416912c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544776}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "7f69989d-58f3-5c44-9cd6-bba8083f79ff" :question/math-academy-id "q-66832" :question/problem "Find the exact solution to the equation $3({4}^{y})-14=19.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({4}^{y})-14 & =19 \\\\ 3({4}^{y}) & =33 \\\\ {4}^{y} & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{4}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{4}⁡({4}^{y}) & ={log}_{4}⁡(11) \\\\ y & ={log}_{4}⁡(11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y={log}_{4}⁡(11).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064a3c82-ae53-5db3-ad5c-b3fcfc6fb6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{5}⁡(4)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544101} {:answer/id #uuid "49f84153-b03e-5266-a48d-c82f2db5b6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544247} {:answer/id #uuid "7b506411-a799-5138-a14f-4b0c6672b0c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)+7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544360} {:answer/id #uuid "cd3750bd-081d-5764-9284-5e0451f625eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544522} {:answer/id #uuid "ee944174-45cf-5629-b838-1acad19f5360" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(7)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49f84153-b03e-5266-a48d-c82f2db5b6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544247} :answer-field/id #uuid "3300a13e-fe37-59f5-9d51-81da8e4c45f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "07d6770c-e373-5366-b946-966ce2aa6000" :question/math-academy-id "q-100163" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation ${7}^{x+4}=5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take ${log}_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{x+4} & =5 \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡({7}^{x+4}) & ={log}_{7}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+4={log}_{7}⁡(5)\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+4 & ={log}_{7}⁡(5) \\\\ x & ={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x={log}_{7}⁡(5)-4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f147060-2e3d-530e-8605-1ba13a4114d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{5}⁡(3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544364} {:answer/id #uuid "9dec9e09-3ab9-51d5-93f5-5553f7a2ae1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{5}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{3}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544429} {:answer/id #uuid "cd163f76-39be-503b-8e02-0fc0fc56c0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{3}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544521} {:answer/id #uuid "d87bd39e-276b-5919-ae48-a488a12d6528" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{{log}_{3}⁡(5)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544553} {:answer/id #uuid "f4426217-c85d-5fd5-a049-5d1b721018a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{3}⁡\\left(\\frac{1}{5}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd163f76-39be-503b-8e02-0fc0fc56c0ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x={log}_{3}⁡(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544521} :answer-field/id #uuid "479444fd-611e-5a03-bcad-55f19ebf647d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544681}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "4dbd2fd5-279c-5b4f-83af-6acbee35f908" :question/math-academy-id "q-66801" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation ${3}^{x}=5.$" :question/worked-solution "We take ${log}_{3}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & =5 \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡({3}^{x}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that ${log}_{b}⁡({b}^{c})=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx={log}_{3}⁡(5)\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "249cec14-666a-5fae-9615-1544a0eec215" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544166} {:answer/id #uuid "3755bb99-c614-5cf1-80fc-6be88288dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544208} {:answer/id #uuid "767e7c4e-ad51-5769-a990-6385b5908531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.260" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544349} {:answer/id #uuid "b73616bd-6754-5514-aa8a-eead41959119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.740" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544475} {:answer/id #uuid "f6221a2d-763a-5c87-bb34-2b68cf8fa1c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.740" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3755bb99-c614-5cf1-80fc-6be88288dbde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.370" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544208} :answer-field/id #uuid "51e41568-3547-5b0e-b361-b42d6abf90f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "7e1ee8c2-d8a9-5564-8fe2-55ce248be31a" :question/math-academy-id "q-31891" :question/problem "Given that ${5}^{2a+3}-13=25,$ find the value of $a$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2a+3}-13 & =25 \\\\ {5}^{2a+3} & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{5}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{5}^{2a+3} & =38 \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡({5}^{2a+3}) & ={log}_{5}⁡(38) \\\\ 2a+3 & ={log}_{5}⁡(38)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3 & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(38)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)} \\\\ 2a & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(38)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}-3 \\\\ a & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(38)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(5)}-\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\na≈-0.370\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544846 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21a7be4c-c258-5104-8444-2a5ac6bf1461" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.685" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544163} {:answer/id #uuid "78981f9f-c8a0-501c-a93c-1f3d6d8a9843" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.604" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544355} {:answer/id #uuid "ca20cb11-444e-5551-a283-109595f4bfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544511} {:answer/id #uuid "d6441217-85f1-5384-af07-4fb4353c7e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544544} {:answer/id #uuid "ddefe1b3-5955-5cb7-9393-02639a571285" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.604" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6441217-85f1-5384-af07-4fb4353c7e2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.842" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544544} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb33b195-f963-5860-8754-612425a1f549" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544777}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "918c847a-dee1-5e90-aa75-e08ca9d39fd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-66811" :question/problem "Given that ${3}^{4-2x}=\\sqrt{2},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking ${log}_{3}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{4-2x} & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡({3}^{4-2x}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 4-2x & ={log}_{3}⁡({2}^{1/2})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n4-2x=\\frac{1}{2}{log}_{3}⁡(2)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)} \\\\ -2x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}-4 \\\\ x & =2-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈1.842\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186544881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10304769-0b45-5ddb-960a-5561ac8890cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.141" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544119} {:answer/id #uuid "26a853f4-f0a8-5a09-b9c0-56c7fc01358d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.115" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544174} {:answer/id #uuid "66790320-0c2c-5cc3-b140-997d9491efef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.981" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544309} {:answer/id #uuid "945201fd-0d4a-5e7f-a3b1-d14b90583f75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.454" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544412} {:answer/id #uuid "feaf6731-e3b7-599f-a042-7ed2790987cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "feaf6731-e3b7-599f-a042-7ed2790987cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.885" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544643} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4daa940-75d3-59a9-9409-b1cafb9f426c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186544774}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "d436286b-8ea5-5b92-b174-4ebb9b14bf53" :question/math-academy-id "q-973" :question/problem "Given that ${11}^{4-y}=\\sqrt[4]{3},$ find the value of $y$  rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking ${log}_{11}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{11}^{4-y} & =\\sqrt[4]{3} \\\\ {log}_{11}⁡({11}^{4-y}) & ={log}_{11}⁡(\\sqrt[4]{3}) \\\\ 4-y & ={log}_{11}⁡({3}^{1/4})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n4-y=\\frac{1}{4}{log}_{11}⁡(3)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4-y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} \\\\ -y & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}-4 \\\\ y & =4-\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}{4\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈3.885\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186569966 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "014ac208-df51-5c62-a006-7a4b9940094f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.527" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569448} {:answer/id #uuid "6d3ecb1e-79b9-5c0c-8d13-23fcec2c2084" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.176" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569617} {:answer/id #uuid "6e72282c-66ef-50e5-a1aa-f7ce5f8bbebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.631" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569621} {:answer/id #uuid "a121dafc-2f1c-5f9d-9334-83be1e4a3593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569699} {:answer/id #uuid "de3f796d-328d-51b3-a6f9-559142e7a197" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569797}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e72282c-66ef-50e5-a1aa-f7ce5f8bbebe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.631" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569621} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58ba2f4-b668-5a8c-92f5-c9264d481c97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "19a2dc0a-21a4-5b89-85c8-47422a295e17" :question/math-academy-id "q-974" :question/problem "Given that $\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {3}^{x}=5,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot {3}^{x} & =5 \\\\ {3}^{x} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{3}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{3}^{x} & =2 \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡({3}^{x}) & ={log}_{3}⁡(2) \\\\ x & ={log}_{3}⁡(2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(2)}{\\operatorname{log}⁡(3)}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.631\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570033 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "310d0146-d260-5636-89ab-ecc12e622eae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.353" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569514} {:answer/id #uuid "437278c9-7a76-5f2e-b4a6-02500ee6a3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.335" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569537} {:answer/id #uuid "7d7a2b6a-8f01-536e-a4bb-dec07965bb90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.533" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569651} {:answer/id #uuid "9be72108-4bdd-5fab-a923-17cc67035375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.303" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569692} {:answer/id #uuid "c72edcf4-d019-51c5-b9b0-7370b8b2c4d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.350" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "437278c9-7a76-5f2e-b4a6-02500ee6a3f2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.335" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569537} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8491df2-d5c3-5271-8329-efe669739dd5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e0b9a214-575e-56bc-9016-1d953bb568c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-100254" :question/problem "Given that ${7}^{5x}+8=34,$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{5x}+8 & =34 \\\\ {7}^{5x} & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take ${log}_{7}$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{7}^{5x} & =26 \\\\ {log}_{7}⁡({7}^{5x}) & ={log}_{7}⁡(26) \\\\ 5x & ={log}_{7}⁡(26) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}{log}_{7}⁡(26)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.335\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186570041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f642b7e-3aa4-589d-b5d0-69cd84cc61e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.041" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569466} {:answer/id #uuid "4e71bb66-f31b-56f1-8b96-dceb6bb51802" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.911" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569553} {:answer/id #uuid "6a7282e0-ffd3-5bad-a6f6-578fd6e4195e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.041" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569610} {:answer/id #uuid "9762dcaa-9d7a-5565-8692-82ad8a90275e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.771" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569682} {:answer/id #uuid "b59296e7-69ea-5b0f-8c88-fdca508c6ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.771" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569731}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b59296e7-69ea-5b0f-8c88-fdca508c6ae7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.771" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569731} :answer-field/id #uuid "335d885a-d13c-55bb-8478-3d052924914c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186569864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fa39cf5e-b1cf-510a-a444-4f30da1c63f4" :question/math-academy-id "q-66814" :question/problem "Given that ${11}^{2x-3}=\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{2}},$  find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Taking ${log}_{11}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{11}^{2x-3} & =\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{2}} \\\\ {log}_{11}⁡({11}^{2x-3}) & ={log}_{11}⁡(\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{2}}) \\\\ 2x-3 & ={log}_{11}⁡({7}^{2/3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n2x-3=\\frac{2}{3}{log}_{11}⁡(7)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)} \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}+3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}⁡(7)}{3\\operatorname{log}⁡(11)}+\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈1.771\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607726 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3caa3058-f371-524c-b4c0-5813f1e550bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.907" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607735} {:answer/id #uuid "6741d9ab-bac7-508e-a5b3-601f8a3730be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.882" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607738} {:answer/id #uuid "789a27f5-c668-532f-bd13-290a2b610c55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.901" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607741} {:answer/id #uuid "98456add-a0c9-5cf9-8cb0-d8297dbb0c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.860" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607745} {:answer/id #uuid "eab84d11-58e7-52b2-afb6-7145763089ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.916" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607755}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98456add-a0c9-5cf9-8cb0-d8297dbb0c9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.860" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607745} :answer-field/id #uuid "7942c58a-97b4-5d34-aa59-6db2b29a0735" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607742}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0d404f08-caf9-5bc9-a919-905910d2c01f" :question/problem "Given that $10^{-4-5x}=\\sqrt{4},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{10}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10^{-4-5x} &= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n\\log_{10}\\left(10^{-4-5x}\\right) &= \\log_{10}\\left(\\sqrt{4}\\right) \\\\\n-4-5x &= \\log_{10}\\left(4^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n-4-5x=\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{10}(4)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4-5x &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{2\\log(10)} \\\\\n-5x &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{2\\log(10)}+4 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{\\log(4)}{10\\log(10)}-\\frac{4}{5}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx -0.860\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607728 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e6e2c15-106e-5ae2-a1d7-f4413d796b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.807" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607732} {:answer/id #uuid "74836772-e835-546b-a145-adb685117333" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.808" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607740} {:answer/id #uuid "7b86698e-8ed6-5c96-8174-ec0e662cdca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.773" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607743} {:answer/id #uuid "db778dc7-12bf-57a4-aaa8-1f3fec03195a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.789" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607753} {:answer/id #uuid "e5b24206-1480-5d59-93b1-17c582f9d624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.796" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607754}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5b24206-1480-5d59-93b1-17c582f9d624" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.796" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607754} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e416c51-24c6-556c-a1a1-b7b77e674c8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607731}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1007bd14-808d-5a46-93e3-9b140f1d68c8" :question/problem "Given that $6^{3x-2}=\\sqrt{4},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n6^{3x-2} &= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n\\log_{6}\\left(6^{3x-2}\\right) &= \\log_{6}\\left(\\sqrt{4}\\right) \\\\\n3x-2 &= \\log_{6}\\left(4^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n3x-2=\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{6}(4)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x-2 &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{2\\log(6)} \\\\\n3x &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{2\\log(6)}+2 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{6\\log(6)}+\\frac{2}{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx 0.796\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607733 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f70c6ce-70c0-5722-afcf-a2280f3cabe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.962" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607727} {:answer/id #uuid "38e85232-b60a-5f49-870e-b204a4afa754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.874" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607734} {:answer/id #uuid "9d2b9963-42ae-5be6-a502-95c7a107feec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.073" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607746} {:answer/id #uuid "aad1813f-37cb-56f6-b582-f0d2c9e030f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.683" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607749} {:answer/id #uuid "b702efc5-f595-56a3-be19-07ec988c6e2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.781" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607750}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aad1813f-37cb-56f6-b582-f0d2c9e030f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.683" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607749} :answer-field/id #uuid "64824a20-c3ee-5e93-8d24-5e3072ea31ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "34cedd9e-990e-5ec9-ad41-ad4ee3d8fcce" :question/problem "Given that $11^{-2y+4}=\\sqrt{21},$ find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{11}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n11^{-2y+4} &= \\sqrt{21} \\\\\n\\log_{11}\\left(11^{-2y+4}\\right) &= \\log_{11}\\left(\\sqrt{21}\\right) \\\\\n-2y+4 &= \\log_{11}\\left(21^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n-2y+4=\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{11}(21)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2y+4 &= \\frac{\\log(21)}{2\\log(11)} \\\\\n-2y &= \\frac{\\log(21)}{2\\log(11)}-4 \\\\\ny &= -\\frac{\\log(21)}{4\\log(11)}+2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny\\approx 1.683\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607739 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29d4dcac-781a-52ac-9e4a-1f59138b7096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.293" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607730} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd4fedb-d452-50e8-9eb4-7f06848f52b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.277" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607744} {:answer/id #uuid "aa0d4f33-e46f-5420-abab-dbc46dc90778" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607748} {:answer/id #uuid "d2758e4c-b3ef-5e80-9821-b3a78ec06a72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "