" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.324" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607736} {:answer/id #uuid "a675c78f-c003-5090-83d6-5f38eb0f7e8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.311" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607747} {:answer/id #uuid "d354fc10-debe-5597-b8b8-33dc9595bfc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.319" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607752} {:answer/id #uuid "f9b8502d-c013-5b20-ab11-4364d33b85bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.302" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29c45cb6-ee7b-5ceb-adfc-bddc75f891ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.333" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607729} :answer-field/id #uuid "f03b0866-f0de-5392-878b-ffcb1f0ed8a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f77971b5-f151-56ac-b168-a1f3a19b62d1" :question/problem "Given that $8^{-2x+5}=\\sqrt{4},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{8}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n8^{-2x+5} &= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n\\log_{8}\\left(8^{-2x+5}\\right) &= \\log_{8}\\left(\\sqrt{4}\\right) \\\\\n-2x+5 &= \\log_{8}\\left(4^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n-2x+5=\\frac{1}{2}\\log_{8}(4)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x+5 &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{2\\log(8)} \\\\\n-2x &= \\frac{\\log(4)}{2\\log(8)}-5 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{\\log(4)}{4\\log(8)}+\\frac{5}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx 2.333\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607763 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "169cd12e-8b0a-559a-bd7c-0fb4b7d94eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_{9}\\left(22\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607766} {:answer/id #uuid "45d476f1-2c0a-5fac-a760-d2f9c102ccf9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_{9}\\left(10\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607775} {:answer/id #uuid "4a90aa41-1985-5df9-b0ff-0e450a6ae374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_{9}\\left(14\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607776} {:answer/id #uuid "56b39aa1-21ee-567d-86ce-af29f3ae4451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_{9}\\left(20\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607777} {:answer/id #uuid "60ad4f9a-52aa-5295-a833-bc2c0766d018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_{9}\\left(18\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607781}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60ad4f9a-52aa-5295-a833-bc2c0766d018" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_{9}\\left(18\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607781} :answer-field/id #uuid "035e7f45-32f4-534b-b2b9-d9bc07849575" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607762}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0683482e-de86-5ea0-ba32-cd532ad3ecb3" :question/problem "Find the exact solution to the equation $\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 9^{y}-12=15$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 9^{y}-12&=15 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}\\cdot 9^{y}&=27 \\\\ 9^{y}&=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{9}\\left(9^{y}\\right)&=\\log_{9}\\left(18\\right) \\\\ y&=\\log_{9}\\left(18\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=\\log_{9}\\left(18\\right)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607770 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e3ef766-bc53-56ac-acf8-9d6213a15e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.328" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607765} {:answer/id #uuid "3a388797-2a5b-52c5-9b47-41e290e061fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.188" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607772} {:answer/id #uuid "581ab1f0-6c9e-5602-bdae-a11f97c2c9d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.774" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607778} {:answer/id #uuid "5c6844e0-9b9f-5308-9235-a281abbb8219" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.285" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607779} {:answer/id #uuid "85af5bb3-0a63-54a5-a8f2-8ede41bf18ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.649" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607786}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "85af5bb3-0a63-54a5-a8f2-8ede41bf18ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.649" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607786} :answer-field/id #uuid "26d3df75-11b9-59ae-9341-2da97ccaf04e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607769}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2a662c01-a263-583a-8b6d-f56b28176db0" :question/problem "Given that $5\\cdot 6^{a}=16$, find the value of $a$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\cdot 6^{a}&=16 \\\\ 6^{a}&=\\frac{16}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{6}\\left(6^{a}\\right)&=\\log_{6}\\left(\\frac{16}{5}\\right) \\\\ a&=\\log_{6}\\left(\\frac{16}{5}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a&=\\frac{\\log\\left(\\frac{16}{5}\\right)}{\\log\\left(6\\right)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\na\\approx 0.649\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186607771 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07bc4c24-064f-5e64-933c-505e540fa1b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.352" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607764} {:answer/id #uuid "1d7f5a33-81e2-5068-947f-23edf35cb36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.276" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607768} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd87f4c-2e28-5833-a3b4-4bc9eea5d2c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.650" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607785} {:answer/id #uuid "cade2123-62a5-51d9-a883-b149fe6f1372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.591" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607792} {:answer/id #uuid "f4cf13ce-9c74-5319-b803-dcda04b76fd0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.570" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186607794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d7f5a33-81e2-5068-947f-23edf35cb36b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answ