$$\na\\approx 1.040\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186653068 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53b750a1-8105-5e33-9337-52923d87b0d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_4(7)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653062} {:answer/id #uuid "54b5c430-53fb-585d-9b74-100c2bc3eff1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_4(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653063} {:answer/id #uuid "6f42eeb6-c582-5d6a-ae51-c64831537082" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\frac{\\log_4(7)}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653064} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1b6242-0822-57a3-9079-17b3964c9f0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_4(7)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653065} {:answer/id #uuid "edaf6372-97f4-5c6d-9fcb-21c5c8075fd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_7(4)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b750a1-8105-5e33-9337-52923d87b0d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_4(7)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653062} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bf2134a-3874-5cc1-a766-7b0ab88d1f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186653067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2dd924e4-dd60-54b1-9a1e-93f6380c91b5" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $4^{x-3}=7$." :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_4$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4^{x-3}&=7\\\\\n\\log_4\\left(4^{x-3}\\right)&=\\log_4(7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ gives $x-3=\\log_4(7)$. Adding $3$ to both sides, we obtain\n\n$$\nx=\\log_4(7)+3.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186655643 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "211ecb65-919d-5b34-a357-a2bac1136537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{9}(11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655644} {:answer/id #uuid "82daa7c3-9d37-5089-8dae-d710f8dd15ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{3}(16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655657} {:answer/id #uuid "87650e62-518e-56e9-b7f5-54ae89d192b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{9}(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655659} {:answer/id #uuid "90446ac5-81f1-532f-b4e3-34047bde6de7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{3}(10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655662} {:answer/id #uuid "d72339ad-ce21-57a4-b1a6-92b1794ce27b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{3}(11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655669}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "211ecb65-919d-5b34-a357-a2bac1136537" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{9}(11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655644} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5e41df6-6e9f-5867-b89b-4bf1c40be1ee" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655665}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1e822cbb-205f-5838-a341-7e93ec09d4d5" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $9^{x}=11.$" :question/worked-solution "We take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9^{x}&=11\\\\\\log_{9}(9^{x})&=\\log_{9}(11)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx=\\log_{9}(11).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{9}(11)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186655649 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "511c95b6-00a4-5ce5-a368-b2d32bbb5a5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{7}(14)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655647} {:answer/id #uuid "7dd314e6-fd12-54f7-b5e8-84fe7bfa7d04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{7}(14)-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655656} {:answer/id #uuid "cffa898c-9f38-557b-be51-389724a0f917" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{2}(20)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655667} {:answer/id #uuid "e1cc3b71-7b51-536c-ab82-781b255363a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{2}(20)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655671} {:answer/id #uuid "f8ee34e2-b6eb-5e47-a1cc-de5a098f5b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{7}(20)-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655674}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8ee34e2-b6eb-5e47-a1cc-de5a098f5b66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{7}(20)-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655674} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bf32041-f68d-5645-8e41-4a054e8a9a2f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655641}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5c4943ae-854f-5c47-b280-b29ef9dcacec" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $7^{x+5}=20.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7^{x+5}&=20\\\\\\log_{7}(7^{x+5})&=\\log_{7}(20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+5=\\log_{7}(20).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+5&=\\log_{7}(20)\\\\x&=\\log_{7}(20)-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{7}(20)-5$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186655658 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a59d3ac-5bbc-54c5-99e0-d21a819ca50a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{8}(32)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655646} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf20b41-be30-5c36-93e1-1b3c95884af5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(21)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655653} {:answer/id #uuid "77f7b9a3-1d66-5959-836d-0bcf66c15ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(32)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655654} {:answer/id #uuid "96f1a570-29f3-589b-ab16-c63c3c926544" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{8}(21)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655663} {:answer/id #uuid "de89987e-a1e6-50bc-be96-d274c748ec08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(28)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77f7b9a3-1d66-5959-836d-0bcf66c15ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(32)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655654} :answer-field/id #uuid "79494a10-bccb-5060-913e-1a370bd752dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "845b2265-ac43-56eb-a745-7ede0da24fe1" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $6^{x}=32.$" :question/worked-solution "We take $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6^{x}&=32\\\\\\log_{6}(6^{x})&=\\log_{6}(32)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx=\\log_{6}(32).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{6}(32)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186655660 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10bc9205-05dc-5109-86d3-766644bba1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{5}(20)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655642} {:answer/id #uuid "656c2561-23ae-578b-93a6-ada4db3ca262" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(20)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655652} {:answer/id #uuid "8f034615-0d9a-5afd-8b8f-c892030a731c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(24)-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655661} {:answer/id #uuid "d0689f58-d64b-5ec3-8c75-8b469ecee346" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(24)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655668} {:answer/id #uuid "f1381e5d-e150-5938-9a74-6348c18dd2c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(24)+3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "10bc9205-05dc-5109-86d3-766644bba1b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{5}(20)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655642} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9399b1a-3983-57ac-895e-34f484b8fe50" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8bcda31d-628f-5bb0-87e5-685461ff59ea" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $5^{x-2}=20.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_{5}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5^{x-2}&=20\\\\\\log_{5}(5^{x-2})&=\\log_{5}(20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx-2=\\log_{5}(20).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-2&=\\log_{5}(20)\\\\x&=\\log_{5}(20)+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{5}(20)+2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186655664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06e44fa2-8eed-5b7d-86b5-8fecd855c5bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(21)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655640} {:answer/id #uuid "247a1552-2454-52d5-b9fb-7c21fcb13202" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{6}(40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655645} {:answer/id #uuid "591608b2-bab9-5f62-ad2e-4ecc2173bd7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{8}(40)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655648} {:answer/id #uuid "6320f863-4f79-5097-abb2-8dbdd127b184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{8}(20)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655651} {:answer/id #uuid "efa8db03-11b6-5607-a3bb-85bd8d346362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{8}(21)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655672}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "efa8db03-11b6-5607-a3bb-85bd8d346362" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_{8}(21)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655672} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe93ea4-b6f7-5c53-a5be-510635bd1073" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186655650}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "99ea5249-5792-56f1-b1f6-d87ea0a2cc7e" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $8^{x}=21.$" :question/worked-solution "We take $\\log_{8}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8^{x}&=21\\\\\\log_{8}(8^{x})&=\\log_{8}(21)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx=\\log_{8}(21).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{8}(21)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b2be22d-388b-5a98-bc8a-5fd8e3d042a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688644} {:answer/id #uuid "82a9d6cb-a159-574d-8015-e1b88d8fa694" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688651} {:answer/id #uuid "b451ca2f-c368-53e7-bdc1-41c6ce4b829b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688655} {:answer/id #uuid "d3453aca-da53-5723-a411-3f7731db494d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688658} {:answer/id #uuid "e75c970e-cc5e-5056-9b1e-5863cff2ed71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3453aca-da53-5723-a411-3f7731db494d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.292" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688658} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f2f1758-3837-5dff-a593-0438318396cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1c67d181-29ca-5005-9df8-871dc9065249" :question/problem "Given that $3\\cdot 4^{2x+1}+5=32$, find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, subtract $5$ and divide by $3$ to isolate the exponential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3\\cdot 4^{2x+1}+5 &= 32 \\\\\n3\\cdot 4^{2x+1} &= 27 \\\\\n4^{2x+1} &= 9.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the logarithm with base $4$ of both sides, then solve the resulting linear equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_4(4^{2x+1}) &= \\log_4(9) \\\\\n2x+1 &= \\log_4(9) \\\\\n2x &= \\log_4(9)-1 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{\\log_4(9)-1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the change of base formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{\\log(9)}{\\log(4)}-1\\right)\\approx 0.2924812504.\n$$\n\nKeep the calculator's full precision until the final step. Rounded to $3$ decimal places, $x\\approx 0.292$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67e447c1-9766-5bee-8bef-33bd2341012b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_5(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688646} {:answer/id #uuid "75c4c080-f8e3-5886-80b6-0da3deeb6688" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_7(5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688647} {:answer/id #uuid "81d2733b-a8db-593f-b642-bb5ba15df094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_5\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688650} {:answer/id #uuid "8a1c122b-ced4-574f-94cc-02a7e3a640ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=4\\log_5(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688652} {:answer/id #uuid "bad702af-7f99-5aca-83db-96f93fb0e882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_5(28)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "67e447c1-9766-5bee-8bef-33bd2341012b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=\\log_5(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688646} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb47736a-35c5-5df9-8c14-53b23eaf1642" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688657}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "957b4fad-b7d9-51c3-b65d-ccc6e027256b" :question/problem "Find the exact solution to the equation $4\\cdot 5^y-7=21$." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "First, isolate the exponential by adding $7$ and then dividing by $4$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4\\cdot 5^y-7 &= 21 \\\\\n4\\cdot 5^y &= 28 \\\\\n5^y &= 7.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the logarithm with base $5$ on both sides. Since $\\log_5(5^y)=y$,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_5(5^y) &= \\log_5(7) \\\\\ny &= \\log_5(7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe exact solution is $y=\\log_5(7)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688654 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0045628b-6384-54ba-baa3-62c029f895a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.232" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688641} {:answer/id #uuid "30ff1930-667b-53fe-8c86-bfea7a8bbcb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688643} {:answer/id #uuid "6393a8f2-0500-54e6-85cf-9ae50de401e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.512" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688645} {:answer/id #uuid "7b4084b2-7e94-5e9a-a788-56eed5f432ef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.244" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688648} {:answer/id #uuid "e7ab474a-10ae-5dc5-b01d-741aedb49d62" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30ff1930-667b-53fe-8c86-bfea7a8bbcb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688643} :answer-field/id #uuid "da9e0586-4c36-5216-b50f-64fe53cc2c4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688659}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9912419b-bbc8-5860-b6de-fa5efa54f0e6" :question/problem "Given that $2\\cdot 3^{1-2x}=\\sqrt[3]{40}$, find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Divide both sides by $2$ to isolate the exponential. Since $40=8\\cdot 5$, we have $\\sqrt[3]{40}=2\\sqrt[3]{5}$, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2\\cdot 3^{1-2x} &= \\sqrt[3]{40} \\\\\n3^{1-2x} &= \\frac{\\sqrt[3]{40}}{2} \\\\\n3^{1-2x} &= \\sqrt[3]{5}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTake the logarithm with base $3$ on both sides. Rewrite the cube root as a power and use the logarithm power rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_3(3^{1-2x}) &= \\log_3(\\sqrt[3]{5}) \\\\\n1-2x &= \\log_3(5^{1/3}) \\\\\n1-2x &= \\frac{1}{3}\\log_3(5).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow solve for $x$ and use the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x &= \\frac{1}{3}\\log_3(5)-1 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{6}\\log_3(5) \\\\\nx &= \\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{\\log(5)}{6\\log(3)} \\\\\nx &\\approx 0.2558377465.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRound only at the end. To $3$ decimal places, $x\\approx 0.256$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e10c8c5-1f64-58be-9689-b9ac51a60662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.183" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688992} {:answer/id #uuid "723d14c5-cbc1-5bde-a36a-4a30f8e7136b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.099" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689003} {:answer/id #uuid "d7b64230-162d-55f4-9f4f-a68feb98b332" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.048" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689012} {:answer/id #uuid "e3469c9d-c8e1-5687-8de3-9339341719fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.153" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689013} {:answer/id #uuid "e643a742-dc6e-56ab-ad6c-9f21b2c277e7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.025" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e10c8c5-1f64-58be-9689-b9ac51a60662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.183" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688992} :answer-field/id #uuid "0da0b6d2-6c0c-581f-b91f-4e3cb6004377" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "0260e677-70ba-533f-bc33-07516b7680db" :question/problem "Given that $4^{6a+3}+17=31$, find the value of $a$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4^{6a+3}+17&=31 \\\\ 4^{6a+3}&=14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{4}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{4}\\left(4^{6a+3}\\right)&=\\log_{4}\\left(14\\right) \\\\ 6a+3&=\\log_{4}\\left(14\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6a+3&=\\frac{\\log\\left(14\\right)}{\\log\\left(4\\right)} \\\\ 6a&=\\frac{\\log\\left(14\\right)}{\\log\\left(4\\right)}-3 \\\\ a&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(14\\right)}{\\log\\left(4\\right)}-3}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\na\\approx -0.183\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688993 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ec71396-ffb8-5422-bc49-becdb5e9da3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.389" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688998} {:answer/id #uuid "6aa83f00-deb2-5019-886e-5c12da0dc316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.613" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689001} {:answer/id #uuid "98dc1c9e-3691-58df-828a-3a6b18904c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.494" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689007} {:answer/id #uuid "b887177d-3ba5-5adf-9c19-b24617600176" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.462" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689010} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a680dc-75b2-5804-b994-68fabb062e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.364" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98dc1c9e-3691-58df-828a-3a6b18904c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.494" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689007} :answer-field/id #uuid "405aab1a-eac4-53ef-b683-6cdab9ea3095" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688995}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "214336c9-de40-5ae8-a3bb-ff822df675eb" :question/problem "Given that $9^{3y}+12=38$, find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9^{3y}+12&=38 \\\\ 9^{3y}&=26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{9}\\left(9^{3y}\\right)&=\\log_{9}\\left(26\\right) \\\\ 3y&=\\log_{9}\\left(26\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y&=\\frac{\\log\\left(26\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)} \\\\ y&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(26\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny\\approx 0.494\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688994 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c6543f-b43b-597e-9f05-620a4b28fb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.327" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688996} {:answer/id #uuid "71f108e2-d11c-5947-a0e1-b429be2f5383" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.313" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689002} {:answer/id #uuid "7acc8962-a28d-574e-898a-dbf9b989878c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.323" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689004} {:answer/id #uuid "8bef0197-b9f2-53a2-8d2e-7c91c709c889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.247" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689006} {:answer/id #uuid "e9a7c8fb-5b2c-5d98-9fa5-6d795d63c98a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bef0197-b9f2-53a2-8d2e-7c91c709c889" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.247" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689006} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a08d222-c343-54a2-8aea-9951825119b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "2ed4b954-2b3a-582c-a13a-83024602ace1" :question/problem "Given that $9^{6x}-17=9$, find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9^{6x}-17&=9 \\\\ 9^{6x}&=26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{9}\\left(9^{6x}\\right)&=\\log_{9}\\left(26\\right) \\\\ 6x&=\\log_{9}\\left(26\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x&=\\frac{\\log\\left(26\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)} \\\\ x&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(26\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx 0.247\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186688997 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5f74b46f-3684-5b72-a6c4-ed35c559387c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.341" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186688999} {:answer/id #uuid "87b218d9-47ba-5933-b047-cfd9637e2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.465" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689005} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a3b24a-b820-517c-aadf-46c4dbcda015" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.579" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689008} {:answer/id #uuid "aab75098-f0bb-5ca3-b57f-0d0b797b21b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.456" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689009} {:answer/id #uuid "f4fe7468-15f9-5d9b-bbd8-067db714a4ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.489" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "87b218d9-47ba-5933-b047-cfd9637e2d43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.465" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689005} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba829d6d-417f-5179-a3dc-ab7bdbdbdbcd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "48d91943-c8f3-5386-a486-d6acdb711c3d" :question/problem "Given that $9^{3y+3}-13=21$, find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9^{3y+3}-13&=21 \\\\ 9^{3y+3}&=34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{9}\\left(9^{3y+3}\\right)&=\\log_{9}\\left(34\\right) \\\\ 3y+3&=\\log_{9}\\left(34\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y+3&=\\frac{\\log\\left(34\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)} \\\\ 3y&=\\frac{\\log\\left(34\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)}-3 \\\\ y&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(34\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)}-3}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny\\approx -0.465\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689019 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044253f7-933b-55fc-855d-13df8fb030a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.679" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689020} {:answer/id #uuid "1636ed61-dca5-5873-a640-c7642fa670bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.877" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689022} {:answer/id #uuid "855b2b48-aa2f-53fb-a6d4-339e32a2ea5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.730" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689031} {:answer/id #uuid "9399619d-369d-5d5d-9252-92d3eacc475e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.941" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689033} {:answer/id #uuid "be54681b-d9dc-595f-a399-0dff4216adc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.453" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "855b2b48-aa2f-53fb-a6d4-339e32a2ea5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.730" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689031} :answer-field/id #uuid "bdfc0c87-7f52-5594-9f4a-fc4c98b042af" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689039}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "0352f84e-c76e-5003-b917-8e29131b7144" :question/problem "Given that $2\\cdot 2^{2a+3}+7=51$, find the value of $a$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 2^{2a+3}+7&=51 \\\\ 2\\cdot 2^{2a+3}&=44 \\\\ 2^{2a+3}&=22\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{2}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{2}\\left(2^{2a+3}\\right)&=\\log_{2}\\left(22\\right) \\\\ 2a+3&=\\log_{2}\\left(22\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $a$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+3&=\\frac{\\log\\left(22\\right)}{\\log\\left(2\\right)} \\\\ 2a&=\\frac{\\log\\left(22\\right)}{\\log\\left(2\\right)}-3 \\\\ a&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(22\\right)}{\\log\\left(2\\right)}-3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\na\\approx 0.730\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f2e0850-263d-54af-8525-10ced8ab4531" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.710" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689024} {:answer/id #uuid "5f189ed9-8784-5117-86af-90da66de989d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.754" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689028} {:answer/id #uuid "8aea9fbd-27df-5754-be2e-102f59795d1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.777" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689032} {:answer/id #uuid "d47b782f-6e01-54cb-aba1-aabb19f99f9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.868" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689042} {:answer/id #uuid "fef8ace5-937b-5f95-9c3b-ef90429a38dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.870" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fef8ace5-937b-5f95-9c3b-ef90429a38dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.870" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689046} :answer-field/id #uuid "c2713f50-e748-5e7d-9bae-77b49be907a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689041}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "13c1b3ac-a412-5617-8e88-dcfeba84c480" :question/problem "Given that $3\\cdot 7^{-3x-1}+1=70$, find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\cdot 7^{-3x-1}+1&=70 \\\\ 3\\cdot 7^{-3x-1}&=69 \\\\ 7^{-3x-1}&=23\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{7}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{7}\\left(7^{-3x-1}\\right)&=\\log_{7}\\left(23\\right) \\\\ -3x-1&=\\log_{7}\\left(23\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x-1&=\\frac{\\log\\left(23\\right)}{\\log\\left(7\\right)} \\\\ -3x&=\\frac{\\log\\left(23\\right)}{\\log\\left(7\\right)}+1 \\\\ x&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(23\\right)}{\\log\\left(7\\right)}+1}{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx -0.870\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54ac20ea-3e11-5661-9815-17af41ab3122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.488" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689026} {:answer/id #uuid "554f48e9-1c96-56fb-9c9c-5ca5e1cf9cf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.508" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689027} {:answer/id #uuid "9ca5dd67-25c7-5446-83ec-57a54350362e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.228" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689034} {:answer/id #uuid "b65a760b-378a-5b19-99d7-f0e98fb82acd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.244" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689038} {:answer/id #uuid "e597eda1-4e93-5d92-9357-0b5c9c5c6ef7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.389" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54ac20ea-3e11-5661-9815-17af41ab3122" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.488" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689026} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d92d0cb-cc29-5e20-9f75-4acf7698236a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689030}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ac770c00-286a-5e61-a770-372fb9b062e9" :question/problem "Given that $2\\cdot 9^{3y-3}-4=46$, find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot 9^{3y-3}-4&=46 \\\\ 2\\cdot 9^{3y-3}&=50 \\\\ 9^{3y-3}&=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{9}\\left(9^{3y-3}\\right)&=\\log_{9}\\left(25\\right) \\\\ 3y-3&=\\log_{9}\\left(25\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y-3&=\\frac{\\log\\left(25\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)} \\\\ 3y&=\\frac{\\log\\left(25\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)}+3 \\\\ y&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(25\\right)}{\\log\\left(9\\right)}+3}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny\\approx 1.488\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689045 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e4848e6-c535-5e1f-9209-8464af2635dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.602" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689023} {:answer/id #uuid "67a356f9-cb78-5b82-ae3a-1b34523f94fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.692" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689029} {:answer/id #uuid "9d9ed0a1-8ff8-5160-9484-4d3abb9fba5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.645" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689035} {:answer/id #uuid "a022d109-6616-55c8-8a86-bd8baf3aa532" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.701" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689036} {:answer/id #uuid "da8db7c5-ccc6-5363-be20-fcd3447db845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.550" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689043}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e4848e6-c535-5e1f-9209-8464af2635dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.602" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689023} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ed4bb9a-f1f4-50ac-810e-a05a74f7d36c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689025}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ea10d84c-7829-5f87-a813-8339f6d1ae54" :question/problem "Given that $4\\cdot 6^{-3y+3}+1=35$, find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 6^{-3y+3}+1&=35 \\\\ 4\\cdot 6^{-3y+3}&=34 \\\\ 6^{-3y+3}&=\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we take $\\log_{6}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\log_{6}\\left(6^{-3y+3}\\right)&=\\log_{6}\\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right) \\\\ -3y+3&=\\log_{6}\\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3y+3&=\\frac{\\log\\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right)}{\\log\\left(6\\right)} \\\\ -3y&=\\frac{\\log\\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right)}{\\log\\left(6\\right)}-3 \\\\ y&=\\frac{\\frac{\\log\\left(\\frac{17}{2}\\right)}{\\log\\left(6\\right)}-3}{-3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny\\approx 0.602\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689143 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "095a96b8-88c1-51da-8675-42198f44f394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.386" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689140} {:answer/id #uuid "0e830d74-0ca3-5c8e-89d8-38094078e38f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.057" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689141} {:answer/id #uuid "63cda343-b5d2-51c1-9e06-ae567cf1f794" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.359" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689146} {:answer/id #uuid "63d13a40-3ec8-599b-9f11-47e61a5e5378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.943" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689147} {:answer/id #uuid "d270305a-c6cc-5642-86cc-995d93dc476f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.114" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e830d74-0ca3-5c8e-89d8-38094078e38f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.057" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689141} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc98a57a-d49d-57bd-8cbc-4fd27c26404f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689155}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1784b9b0-2fb6-5be6-b159-dc14fe3536d5" :question/problem "Given that $3^{2x+1}=\\sqrt{7}$, find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Take $\\log_3$ of both sides and write the square root as a power:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_3(3^{2x+1})&=\\log_3(\\sqrt{7})\\\\\n2x+1&=\\log_3(7^{1/2}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule, then the change of base formula:\n\n$$\n2x+1=\\frac{1}{2}\\log_3(7)=\\frac{\\log(7)}{2\\log(3)}.\n$$\n\nSubtract $1$ from both sides, then divide the whole right-hand side by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x&=\\frac{\\log(7)}{2\\log(3)}-1\\\\\nx&=\\frac{\\log(7)}{4\\log(3)}-\\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluate without rounding intermediate results. This gives $x\\approx-0.057189$, so $x\\approx-0.057$, rounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689148 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04da45bb-1662-58fb-a764-21eb8ab92123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689139} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3d6160-aa46-57b1-b9bb-53367118615d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.230" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689144} {:answer/id #uuid "7a9671e6-3052-523c-807e-69cc968402ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.568" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689150} {:answer/id #uuid "b200b510-ab1e-5fdb-a479-ad52ad6bdea1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.833" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689153} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ba0369-e25f-5c6f-a336-ea522f9c6100" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.400" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689156}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04da45bb-1662-58fb-a764-21eb8ab92123" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.760" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689139} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d80f9e3-93b8-5b27-aad9-a5a1067b77f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "71e37360-483e-5691-9a47-cfdbc18c7669" :question/problem "Find the solution to the equation $5^y=17$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Take $\\log_5$ of both sides. Since $\\log_5(5^y)=y$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_5(5^y)&=\\log_5(17)\\\\\ny&=\\log_5(17).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the change of base formula to evaluate this with common logarithms:\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{\\log(17)}{\\log(5)}\\approx1.760374.\n$$\n\nThus $y\\approx1.760$, rounded to $3$ decimal places. Keep the full calculator value until the final rounding."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689151 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e97ee53-9832-5a6c-a656-2c9b8bb7e9ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.097" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689142} {:answer/id #uuid "78e5477f-3575-5fe1-a5dd-83e854586a55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7.612" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689149} {:answer/id #uuid "badf8c95-9097-5c9c-90c3-0c3c8b7927b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.164" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689154} {:answer/id #uuid "d94f4445-862d-5a9f-b288-c60e4c12c903" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5.194" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689158} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a4e9c5-cd86-5323-8d98-a139d6485a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.388" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f4a4e9c5-cd86-5323-8d98-a139d6485a3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4.388" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689159} :answer-field/id #uuid "55d81e00-1430-5d23-8387-98ea6d0d96c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689145}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "85e36185-0337-5a8b-b049-80b889617211" :question/problem "Given that $5^{3-y/2}=\\sqrt[3]{7^2}$, find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Take $\\log_5$ of both sides and express the powered cube root using a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_5(5^{3-y/2})&=\\log_5(\\sqrt[3]{7^2})\\\\\n3-\\frac{y}{2}&=\\log_5(7^{2/3}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the power rule and change of base formula. Both the square and the cube root contribute to the factor $2/3$:\n\n$$\n3-\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{2}{3}\\log_5(7)=\\frac{2\\log(7)}{3\\log(5)}.\n$$\n\nSubtract $3$ from both sides, then multiply the whole right-hand side by $-2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-\\frac{y}{2}&=\\frac{2\\log(7)}{3\\log(5)}-3\\\\\ny&=6-\\frac{4\\log(7)}{3\\log(5)}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep full calculator precision until the last step. This gives $y\\approx4.387917$, so $y\\approx4.388$, rounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689426 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cc43493-34ba-504c-9098-2b83c675a365" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.978" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689425} {:answer/id #uuid "714e5997-79d9-5693-aad6-d75588f10378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.886" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689434} {:answer/id #uuid "746ac9a5-f908-5df8-bd52-904c1c257bff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.784" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689435} {:answer/id #uuid "7533b55b-c83f-529d-abf9-fa68e79e9b8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.687" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689436} {:answer/id #uuid "addf3fd1-2d36-584b-9d43-a9a7f82921bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.079" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "addf3fd1-2d36-584b-9d43-a9a7f82921bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.079" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689440} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5933f90-9b78-526d-bdda-536e7a37461a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689439}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "1edd7699-db46-508e-8652-7fcf9e810f47" :question/problem "Given that $3^{-2x-2}=\\sqrt[4]{2},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{3}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^{-2x-2} &= \\sqrt[4]{2} \\\\\n\\log_{3}\\left(3^{-2x-2}\\right) &= \\log_{3}\\left(\\sqrt[4]{2}\\right) \\\\\n-2x-2 &= \\log_{3}\\left(2^{\\frac{1}{4}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n-2x-2=\\frac{1}{4}\\log_{3}(2)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x-2 &= \\frac{\\log(2)}{4\\log(3)} \\\\\n-2x &= \\frac{\\log(2)}{4\\log(3)}+2 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{\\log(2)}{8\\log(3)}-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx -1.079\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689428 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "056db93d-df44-58b8-8379-a2cab182dfb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.119" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689423} {:answer/id #uuid "607918f0-f807-5c3c-aa03-88a35f9443bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.010" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689432} {:answer/id #uuid "9c695505-8ff8-516d-99c4-5c277de1c604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.899" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689437} {:answer/id #uuid "a4b046ac-ec0f-59da-bf19-177be572d047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.809" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689438} {:answer/id #uuid "e2413227-26b1-51b5-8d2f-e950b740eb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.183" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a4b046ac-ec0f-59da-bf19-177be572d047" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.809" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689438} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b8b6d2-7cd2-5437-89ce-652d47415e55" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689443}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "30ae55a7-c98a-5916-b899-444390a3ddd1" :question/problem "Given that $5^{3x+3}=\\sqrt[3]{4^{2}},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{5}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5^{3x+3} &= \\sqrt[3]{4^{2}} \\\\\n\\log_{5}\\left(5^{3x+3}\\right) &= \\log_{5}\\left(\\sqrt[3]{4^{2}}\\right) \\\\\n3x+3 &= \\log_{5}\\left(4^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n3x+3=\\frac{2}{3}\\log_{5}(4)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x+3 &= \\frac{2\\log(4)}{3\\log(5)} \\\\\n3x &= \\frac{2\\log(4)}{3\\log(5)}-3 \\\\\nx &= \\frac{2\\log(4)}{9\\log(5)}-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx -0.809\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689429 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0717c5ba-d056-5739-b6f6-704f162b4eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.497" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689424} {:answer/id #uuid "2a8696b5-785b-5dc2-920d-ed7e7c2d9561" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.358" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689427} {:answer/id #uuid "4a8d8fdb-3c4b-5f69-8b85-5662f7c227ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.424" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689430} {:answer/id #uuid "51dc897e-1184-5dfe-bb36-459022599e61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689431} {:answer/id #uuid "63158df2-f03a-58c4-af40-620ab77e5c77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.564" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689433}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0717c5ba-d056-5739-b6f6-704f162b4eb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.497" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689424} :answer-field/id #uuid "b927c9ee-3d1d-5259-9845-30b4447c2016" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689441}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "33180225-2e1d-536a-9613-ea15f07e020d" :question/problem "Given that $13^{-4x-1}=\\sqrt[3]{45^{2}},$ find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{13}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n13^{-4x-1} &= \\sqrt[3]{45^{2}} \\\\\n\\log_{13}\\left(13^{-4x-1}\\right) &= \\log_{13}\\left(\\sqrt[3]{45^{2}}\\right) \\\\\n-4x-1 &= \\log_{13}\\left(45^{\\frac{2}{3}}\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n-4x-1=\\frac{2}{3}\\log_{13}(45)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-4x-1 &= \\frac{2\\log(45)}{3\\log(13)} \\\\\n-4x &= \\frac{2\\log(45)}{3\\log(13)}+1 \\\\\nx &= -\\frac{\\log(45)}{6\\log(13)}-\\frac{1}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\\approx -0.497\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "213257c3-1fbc-575d-8b3d-62b6e63bbfbf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.589" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689448} {:answer/id #uuid "82463bc8-4a08-5293-baa8-1a5c2c826dfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.613" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689457} {:answer/id #uuid "b85e102c-cfed-5225-b718-fb5ea6849167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.618" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689462} {:answer/id #uuid "ca02dfea-7a96-5f0e-a785-35394c2ff04e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689465} {:answer/id #uuid "ee8f15c7-cc1e-5501-af4e-fd4dc327792a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.586" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca02dfea-7a96-5f0e-a785-35394c2ff04e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.585" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689465} :answer-field/id #uuid "15b3c9e3-63e0-589e-be24-cba58bdf1a2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689446}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "442ac657-3322-562d-a1c5-fa2baa3a6e9e" :question/problem "Given that $2^{z}=3,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{2}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2^{z} &= 3 \\\\\n\\log_{2}\\left(2^{z}\\right) &= \\log_{2}\\left(3\\right) \\\\\nz &= \\log_{2}\\left(3\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= \\frac{\\log(3)}{\\log(2)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz\\approx 1.585\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689455 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cc4b8ed-3696-5938-8a34-6ade813716f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.374" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689450} {:answer/id #uuid "6ed38c7d-279e-5b0b-ace4-0270481da7aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.464" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689456} {:answer/id #uuid "d1f821f4-a45d-5ab1-8147-027b5efe6ef5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.185" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689466} {:answer/id #uuid "d25b10d5-2fad-5974-993a-a941eaabd2d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.099" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689467} {:answer/id #uuid "fb30946a-a3ac-5fbf-9fb5-d59ea9099378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.274" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3cc4b8ed-3696-5938-8a34-6ade813716f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.374" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689450} :answer-field/id #uuid "356cb4dc-6ea9-5889-bdc1-804b0bc79c42" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "68f6ee6f-42b7-5d34-8b07-18c24576d12c" :question/problem "Given that $11^{y}=27,$ find the value of $y$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{11}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n11^{y} &= 27 \\\\\n\\log_{11}\\left(11^{y}\\right) &= \\log_{11}\\left(27\\right) \\\\\ny &= \\log_{11}\\left(27\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\frac{\\log(27)}{\\log(11)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny\\approx 1.374\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689458 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d8c90f4-11c8-538d-92e2-91dda5ac1f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.631" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689447} {:answer/id #uuid "a0f7e6bc-3bf8-5fae-bcdf-db35c0698ba6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.544" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689459} {:answer/id #uuid "c6b85de5-dd05-55cb-b000-02a05fcf4008" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.790" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689464} {:answer/id #uuid "dad0f758-ac2a-5f8e-b37a-fd444fa19060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.698" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689469} {:answer/id #uuid "e6511d95-05cb-5800-9b35-40f05eb90730" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.900" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689470}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d8c90f4-11c8-538d-92e2-91dda5ac1f07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.631" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689447} :answer-field/id #uuid "13f98e26-9eed-5967-aa82-966b15c50b8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689445}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "83871f2f-c8b8-5ef5-9f30-3be9a871320a" :question/problem "Given that $3^{z}=2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{3}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3^{z} &= 2 \\\\\n\\log_{3}\\left(3^{z}\\right) &= \\log_{3}\\left(2\\right) \\\\\nz &= \\log_{3}\\left(2\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= \\frac{\\log(2)}{\\log(3)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz\\approx 0.631\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186689461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49021a13-aa7e-5090-9dbd-de4cdf44acf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.503" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689452} {:answer/id #uuid "580d8230-761a-5be1-8cfa-bf808d63e2e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.696" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689453} {:answer/id #uuid "583ca0d1-b82c-544c-9175-949326d50f0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.439" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689454} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b8a19d-e61c-5600-adab-4a71ac5dc4b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.332" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689460} {:answer/id #uuid "d2d05c88-5ec7-5340-a61a-dcdfab45a94a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.597" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "580d8230-761a-5be1-8cfa-bf808d63e2e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.696" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689453} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3e0f734-5b35-57e4-884e-267632f36583" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186689463}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "b5a8c098-cffa-56c8-97ec-0bb2ec1bfec3" :question/problem "Given that $4^{z}=42,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Taking $\\log_{4}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4^{z} &= 42 \\\\\n\\log_{4}\\left(4^{z}\\right) &= \\log_{4}\\left(42\\right) \\\\\nz &= \\log_{4}\\left(42\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= \\frac{\\log(42)}{\\log(4)}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz\\approx 2.696\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709418 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "588b0aba-140f-56b6-b35f-6711ab493293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "588b0aba-140f-56b6-b35f-6711ab493293" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709421} :answer-field/id #uuid "26e48e52-2920-5033-af2e-022d818e01cb" :answer-field/key "coefficient" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709420} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e60a46cc-dded-5b8c-b5a1-97776e929d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e60a46cc-dded-5b8c-b5a1-97776e929d3d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709431} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd2d9392-1b35-50f4-b680-ff806b12d850" :answer-field/key "constant" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "15ea107b-576e-581e-8c4d-1cef1565483a" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of\n\n$$\n3^{\\frac{1}{2}-x}=\\sqrt[3]{5}.\n$$\n\nExpress the solution in the form $x=a\\log_3(5)+b$, where $a$ and $b$ are rational numbers.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}" :question/worked-solution "Take $\\log_3$ of both sides and use $\\log_b(b^c)=c$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_3\\left(3^{\\frac{1}{2}-x}\\right)&=\\log_3\\left(\\sqrt[3]{5}\\right)\\\\\n\\frac{1}{2}-x&=\\log_3\\left(5^{1/3}\\right).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the power rule $\\log_b(u^r)=r\\log_b(u)$ to put the logarithm in the requested form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}-x=\\frac{1}{3}\\log_3(5).\n$$\n\nSubtract $\\frac{1}{2}$ from both sides, then multiply both sides by $-1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-x&=\\frac{1}{3}\\log_3(5)-\\frac{1}{2}\\\\\nx&=-\\frac{1}{3}\\log_3(5)+\\frac{1}{2}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComparing this with $x=a\\log_3(5)+b$ gives $a=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and $b=\\frac{1}{2}$.\n\nTo check, substitute back: $\\frac{1}{2}-x=\\frac{1}{3}\\log_3(5)$, so $3^{\\frac{1}{2}-x}=\\left(3^{\\log_3(5)}\\right)^{1/3}=\\sqrt[3]{5}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709419 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "741ef7f9-9cb5-58db-8f43-6ab77b1f7b08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=2\\log_2(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709424} {:answer/id #uuid "bb57b1fd-70f2-5334-9b34-a2a5aa157962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_2(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709427} {:answer/id #uuid "c6292c19-f484-57e4-bebd-d0d73778ebd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_7(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709428} {:answer/id #uuid "e3920ddf-9241-53a4-8237-0ade535331f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_2(1/7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709430} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a89795-6b09-5ca3-a4a5-87f7633f83bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=7\\log_2(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709432}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb57b1fd-70f2-5334-9b34-a2a5aa157962" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=\\log_2(7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709427} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e63492b-0b1b-5d36-967a-e21eeb742878" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709425}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "1b52014a-d6a3-5b0a-8e1b-68973449cb7f" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of $2^x=7$." :question/worked-solution "Take $\\log_2$ of both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_2(2^x)&=\\log_2(7)\\\\\nx&=\\log_2(7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere we used $\\log_b(b^c)=c$. Therefore, the exact solution is $x=\\log_2(7)$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709423 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e6c178e-7908-5dc1-b855-b5576f85712a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_3(7)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709426}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e6c178e-7908-5dc1-b855-b5576f85712a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_3(7)+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709426} :answer-field/id #uuid "68b675e1-aae0-580d-b3cf-c5c0d8893531" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "715660d9-9e9e-5f27-9593-6a9d75984d8c" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of $3^{x-2}=7$.\n\n$x=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Take $\\log_3$ of both sides and use $\\log_b(b^c)=c$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\log_3(3^{x-2})&=\\log_3(7)\\\\\nx-2&=\\log_3(7).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd $2$ to both sides to isolate $x$:\n\n$$\nx=\\log_3(7)+2.\n$$\n\nThis is exact; no decimal approximation is needed."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709450 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6390b91-0c54-50b3-b24e-764998a41a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{9}(20)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6390b91-0c54-50b3-b24e-764998a41a56" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{9}(20)-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709462} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bd0a3c4-296c-5445-afbd-0289727ce32e" :answer-field/key "solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "084a6cae-3e51-5fb5-ab3c-aeed476f0b11" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $9^{x+1}=20.$\n\n$x=$ {{solution}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_{9}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9^{x+1}&=20\\\\\\log_{9}(9^{x+1})&=\\log_{9}(20)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+1=\\log_{9}(20).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+1&=\\log_{9}(20)\\\\x&=\\log_{9}(20)-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{9}(20)-1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5009e1ce-0b2a-574e-a579-e9106071f45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{5}(8)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5009e1ce-0b2a-574e-a579-e9106071f45e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{5}(8)-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709455} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c2c86e0-0612-57ff-8923-26640a923d16" :answer-field/key "solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "3d5bf490-5a3a-551d-b5ef-ab2ce0a1867c" :question/problem "Find the exact solution of the equation $5^{x+2}=8.$\n\n$x=$ {{solution}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we take $\\log_{5}$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5^{x+2}&=8\\\\\\log_{5}(5^{x+2})&=\\log_{5}(8)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that $\\log_b(b^c)=c$ to simplify the left-hand side. This gives:\n\n$$\nx+2=\\log_{5}(8).\n$$\n\nFinally, we solve for $x,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2&=\\log_{5}(8)\\\\x&=\\log_{5}(8)-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\log_{5}(8)-2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186709457 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "541924e3-a669-5a9c-8f5c-769319559070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\log_{4}(40)+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186709456}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "541924e3-a669-5a9c-8f5c-769319559070" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/